n\nOperations\n1. Pocket: three round holes of 12 mm, 30 mm deep, for pens and pencils. The tool enters each one in a spiral instead of plunging.\n2. Pocket: a slot 70 x 10 mm, 22 mm deep, for visiting cards or sticky notes.\n3. Profile (outside): cuts the block out with rounded corners, leaving 4 small holding tabs.\n\nBefore cutting for real\n- The holes are deep: enter the flute length of your cutter in the tool's settings and the program warns you if it is too short.\n- Set X0 Y0 at the lower-left corner and Z0 on the top of the stock, and tick \"Air cut\" in each operation for a first run.","act":3,"oid":3}}